sequenceDiagram
    actor User as End User
    participant UI as UI (React console)
    participant CF as CloudFront (/svc/*)
    participant GW as API Gateway
    participant L as Lambda layer
    participant SUP as Supervisor Agent
    participant CA as Credit Analyst Agent
    participant CO as Compliance Agent
    participant S3 as S3 (customer data)
    participant GOV as Gov backends (AVP · Bedrock Guardrails · DynamoDB)

    rect rgb(232,242,254)
    Note over User,GOV: PHASE 1 — Core assessment · produces the REAL decision
    User->>UI: Enter customer_id, run assessment (type=full)
    UI->>GW: POST /api/invoke {customer_id, assessment_type}
    GW->>L: Forward
    L->>SUP: Invoke orchestrator (router branches on assessment_type)
    par Credit path
        SUP->>CA: analyze_credit_risk(customer_id)
        loop Tool-use loop - shown once - framework-provided max 10
            Note over CA: LLM reasons, decides next tool call
            CA->>S3: s3_retriever_tool(profile / credit_history / transactions)
            S3-->>CA: customer data (JSON)
        end
        CA-->>SUP: Credit verdict
    and Compliance path
        SUP->>CO: check_compliance(customer_id)
        Note over CO,S3: Same s3_retriever_tool loop (profile / compliance / transactions)
        CO-->>SUP: Compliance status
    end
    Note over SUP: Synthesize — 1 structured LLM call, no tools
    SUP->>L: Governance review (synthesized assessment)
    Note over L: Non-bypassable: recompute ratios · sanctions/PEP · Cedar cascade · LLM-judge
    L->>S3: Independent re-read (don't trust agent output)
    S3-->>L: Raw data
    L-->>SUP: Decision (APPROVE / ESCALATE / BLOCK + incident_id)
    SUP-->>L: AssessmentResponse
    L-->>GW: AssessmentResponse
    GW-->>UI: 200 {decision, risk, sanctions, checks}
    UI-->>User: Render decision card
    end

    rect rgb(232,250,236)
    Note over User,GOV: PHASE 2 — Console live-badge overlay · ADDITIVE, fire-and-forget · does NOT feed Phase 1 decision
    User->>UI: Advance Basic-mode walkthrough step (scripted narrative)
    Note over UI: Fires live checks using hardcoded scenario FIXTURES, not real output. Failure → badge hidden.
    loop For each governed control on that step (Cedar, grounding, validator, AR, registry, HITL)
        UI->>CF: POST /svc/{control}/... (relative path, NO key)
        Note over CF: injects x-api-key + x-origin-verify at the edge
        CF->>GW: route /svc/* to console-gateway
        GW->>L: proxy to that control's backend Lambda
        L->>GOV: is-authorized / ApplyGuardrail / read table (validator recomputes in-Lambda)
        GOV-->>L: result
        L-->>GW: result
        GW-->>CF: result
        CF-->>UI: verdict
        UI-->>User: light up "verified live" badge (scripted numbers unchanged)
    end
    end
